### A.1 The five supervisor-level questions

Separately from the decision records above, these five questions are the ones that need a supervisor's answer rather than the group's. They are drawn from the parallel gap analysis of the existing proposal and are recorded here so that the outline can be signed off in one meeting.

**Status on the date of this revision: SQ-1, SQ-2, SQ-4 and SQ-5 have been answered by the student and are recorded below as answers. SQ-3 remains open** — it asks for a supervisor's agreement to a change of position (read-only plus approved changes replacing a total exclusion of state-changing actions) and only a supervisor can give that. Where an answer introduces a qualification, **the qualification is recorded, not discarded**: SQ-1's answer is "fully manageable, but introduced incrementally", and §C.6 is what carries the incrementality.

| # | Question | Why it is a supervisor's question | What this outline recommends | Where |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **SQ-1** | **Must the Cisco layer be genuinely manageable by the AI layer, or is a documented simulator gap acceptable?** | **This is the single most important question in the project.** If the answer is "genuinely manageable", Packet Tracer must be replaced or supplemented by a reachable Cisco image — which raises licensing, host-resource and reproducibility questions that the current frozen design forbids by client constraint. If the answer is "a documented gap is acceptable", the AI layer covers two families and the fifth brief line weakens | **ANSWERED — RATIFIED: genuinely manageable. The student's answer is 「期望係完全管理，可逐步加入，非一步到位」** — the expectation is **full management as the destination**, with **incremental introduction rather than all at once**. Therefore: (i) the Cisco layer **must** become genuinely reachable and AI-manageable; this **confirms the primary recommendation (CML)** and **confirms that Packet Tracer cannot be the AI-managed layer**; (ii) the **§C.6 staged AI-coverage ramp** defines how coverage grows, with entry and exit gates per stage; (iii) the **minimum acceptable stage is Stage B** — one genuinely reachable Cisco device, proven end to end — and Stage D (peer-side eBGP verification, impossible today per §C.2b NR-01a) is **explicitly optional and not required within the 12 weeks** | A, C.4, **C.6**, C.5, J-D-01 |
| **SQ-2** | **Where may the local model run, and on what hardware?** | The answer determines the model class, which determines the achievable use cases. The previous design's compute budget sized the AI host at **4 vCPU / 8 GB with no GPU**, which **cannot host a useful local model** — so the compute plan must be re-planned, not inherited | **ANSWERED — DEFERRED, NOT REFUSED.** The student's answer is 「未定，但應有硬件資源，需要待我返港才可安排」: **the resources are expected to exist, but the specific machine and GPU will be arranged when the student returns to Hong Kong.** Consequently: (i) **B1 and D-04 move from blocking now to blocking at gate G2-H, end of week 6**; (ii) a **hardware-agnostic first phase** is added at **§E.1.1a** — the whole network and services layer, the MCP servers and their tests, the agent scaffolding and guardrails, and the evaluation harness all proceed **without any GPU specification**; only the **model class and the serving configuration** wait; (iii) the tier table **T0–T4** and the **no-GPU fallback path** are kept unchanged; (iv) the scheduled decision point is **G2-H**, owner **S4** | E.1, **E.1.1a**, J (B1/D-03/D-04) |
| **SQ-3** | **How far does "manages" go?** | The student has already chosen **read-only plus approved changes**. This **replaces** the previous design's deliberate exclusion of *any* state-changing action, and that change of position carries verification and academic-integrity consequences that need the supervisor's agreement | **STILL OPEN — this is the one question only a supervisor can close.** Recommendation unchanged: **read-only by default; changes only through the six-field proposal → human approval → single-use token → execution → verification → audit workflow.** It is a strength, not a compromise | E.4, E.5, E.8, I.8 |
| **SQ-4** | **Is the AI/MCP layer now the assessed differentiator?** | If yes, the previous framing must be **formally withdrawn** — the corpus currently calls the AI line *"the weakest line"*, treats MCP as cuttable, and places local model serving out of scope. Those statements cannot stand alongside a project whose purpose is AI network management | **ANSWERED — CONFIRMED YES.** The student's answer is 「你可以用呢個方式理解」 to the compound question ("is the AI/MCP layer now the assessed differentiator, **and** should the old framing be formally withdrawn?"), so **both halves are ratified: yes, and yes**. (i) **The AI / MCP layer is the assessed differentiator**; the network is the **foundation it depends on**, not a competitor for the mark. (ii) **The withdrawal of "the AI line is the weakest line" is now definitive and ratified, not a recommendation** — §L.4 W4 carries the strengthened wording. (iii) The standards-alignment argument at §I.4 still argues this honestly: **innovation justified by, but beyond, the WSOS standard** — never a claim of standard compliance | L.4 (**W4**), L.2, I.4 |
| **SQ-5** | **What is the expected submission size and shape now?** | The existing corpus is **286,932 words**, which the gap analysis judges to be two to three times what this project should carry, with 23% of it in one project-management chapter | **ANSWERED — TWO SUBMISSION TIERS, and the immediate one is the proposal alone.** The student's answer is 「暫時只做 proposal」. (i) **Immediate tier = the proposal** — this is the current target, and nothing else is being submitted now. (ii) **Later tier = the full document at 90,000–110,000 words** (hard ceiling 120,000 — a 58–69% cut from 286,932), with the AI / local-model + MCP line growing to about 18,000 words and the implementation-schedule and project-management chapters shrinking hard (for example 66,754 → 15,000–18,000). **This outline is NOT sized to the 6,000–10,000-word outline band — it is a working reference artefact that sits well above it**, at **37,555 whitespace-split words by the canonical method stated at §H.3**, because it doubles as the reachability register, the withdrawal register and the decision log. **§H.3 carries the measurement and the method, and it is the authority on this figure; the outline band applies to the proposal (D5, 15–25 pages), not to this document.** An **initial report** is expected to follow the proposal in the programme's normal sequence: it is recorded at §H.3 as a **likely future deliverable, not current scope**, with its structure `[TO CONFIRM]` against the programme handbook | H.3, L.4 |

